#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""omarchy-touchbar - a context-aware, themed Touch Bar for T2 MacBooks.

tiny-dfr renders whatever is in /etc/tiny-dfr/config.toml and live-reloads it
the moment that file is closed after a write. This daemon listens to Hyprland's
event socket and rewrites that file, so the Touch Bar tracks the focused app,
the workspace you are on, and the windows you have open.

Every button is drawn as a generated SVG, which is the only way to get colour
out of tiny-dfr: text and icon buttons are painted white, but `ButtonImage::Svg`
goes through `render_document`, which keeps the document's own colours. Colours
come from the current Omarchy theme.

  omarchy-touchbar daemon     run the event loop (started from hypr/autostart.lua)
  omarchy-touchbar render     repaint once
  omarchy-touchbar page next|auto|fn|workspaces
  omarchy-touchbar focus N    focus the window in the Nth window slot
  omarchy-touchbar preview    write a PNG mock-up of the bar and print its path
  omarchy-touchbar status     show what the bar is currently showing
"""

